[h1]Glorp UI — Societal Value Hints[/h1]

This mod extends the societal value hint list in Glorp UI. Glorp UI builds that list from government reforms, laws, policies and estate privileges only. The mod adds the remaining sources.

[b]What is added to the list[/b]
[list]
[*] Buildings in the capital
[*] Religious aspects and religious schools
[*] Employment systems
[*] Parliament issues and parliament types
[*] Cabinet actions
[*] International organizations and special statuses in them
[*] Advances
[*] Missions
[*] Subject types
[*] Estates
[*] Chivalric orders
[*] Standing modifiers: fort, army and navy maintenance, army and navy size and experience, average control, average development, literacy, estate shares of the population
[*] Conditional modifiers: war and peace, attacking and defending, bankruptcy, the fort limit, legitimacy, and pointing the cabinet at this value
[/list]

[b]Filter[/b]
The mod removes from the list what your country cannot take: religious aspects of another religion, organizations you cannot join, missions when missions are disabled, parliament issues of an estate you do not have. What will become available once conditions are met is shown in a separate block.
The filter can be turned off in the Community Mod Framework mod menu. The full list is then shown.

[b]Requires[/b]
Glorp UI and Community Mod Framework. Load it after Glorp UI — the launcher does that on its own.

[b]Localization[/b]
English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, Türkçe, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어

[i]The mod and this description were created with the help of an AI. It has been tested as far as was possible.[/i]
